"Olyuk'k is a hot desert-edge region on Artona I, southwest of the art'h siblinghold."
"A large old-fashioned farming village there is an allegiant village, sheltered by one wizard."
"The village is shaped like a wheel, the wizard's home and public buildings at its hub."
"Roads run like spokes to neighborhoods that are small oases clad in historic mud brick."
"Its hexagonal square, the village meet, has rooftop balconies of flat straps reached by ladders."
"The village master's house fills one edge of the square: white domed blobs with curtain walls."
"The village keeps hen fields and a children's school, and o'odee birds are farmed."
"More than half the villagers left in a Here-to-There, moving to another wizard's protection."
"The Here-to-There set out from the village at dawn, guarded by knights of the art'h squad."
"The surrounding desert is hard-packed with spongy plants; deadly bugs are confined by magic."
"Driverless railless trains cross the sand, their front cars holding wizard-class rooms."
"The travelers' destination city is wrapped in a cocoon of flowing sand forming moving pictures."
"That city's station has journey poems on its floor and free food, potion and tablet stalls."
"Its white rooftops swoop like tumbled pillows over balconied streets."
